From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: a file's menu has every such item's verbs and cascading verbs (7502)

The menu listed only the verbs of the items' own type (HKCR\<ProgID>\shell).
As Windows merges them, it now also has the verbs every such item has:
SystemFileAssociations\.ext, * and AllFilesystemObjects for files,
Directory, Folder and AllFilesystemObjects for folders (VS Code's "Open
with Code" is under *), a verb already there not twice. A verb with
SubCommands (the CommandStore's verbs, with CommandFlags separators) or
ExtendedSubCommandsKey (that class's shell verbs) is a submenu: PeaZip's
whole menu is such a cascade and showed nothing. Each verb runs from where
it is registered (its class, or the CommandStore as hkeyClass). Extended
verbs show only with CMF_EXTENDEDVERBS; LegacyDisable,
ProgrammaticAccessOnly and AppliesTo-limited ones are not shown.
---
